content.text:
Mobile title and gameplay:
- Mobile title logo is clipped: "CLOUD HOP" extends beyond screen width (HOP clipped at right? It shows CLOUD HOP but 3D badge overlaps; the logo is within width? Actually "CLOUD HOP" text clipped on left? It looks like starts at x=35 ends x=355, fine; 3D badge at right. Looks okay but main logo overlaps the "SUPER" etc. Title screen fits.
- Controls visible, touch joystick + jump. But top HUD: star counter "0/3" overlaps coin counter? At 390 width: hearts 3 (25px), star 0/3, coin 0/75, timer 0:00.5, mute & pause. The center coin counter overlaps timer? Screenshot shows coin counter, timer, then mute/pause partially cut at right (pause icon maybe off-screen). Indeed the right icons appear clipped: only a mute icon visible at x~370, pause maybe beyond 390. Need fix HUD responsive for narrow widths: hide course label (done); reduce gaps, make timer smaller, maybe hide mute button on mobile? Keep pause. The HUD uses three flex sections; center coin counter plus label; right timer + 2 buttons = ~76+38+38+gaps = 164; left hearts 3*30=90 + star ~50 = 140; center 90; total 394 + padding 32 > 390. Causes overlap/clipping.

Fix for max-width 700: 
- hearts 3 at 22px = 66, star counter compact (hide text? show icon + 0/3 at 12px) ~42.
- coin counter font 18, total 11 ~70.
- timer 16 min-width 58.
- icon buttons 32 each = 64 + gaps 12.
- total 66+42+70+58+64 + gaps ~24 + padding 24 = 348. Good.
- Also allow center shrink.

Additionally on mobile screenshot, top shows the pause button missing/clipped: likely overflow. Fix CSS.

- Touch joystick position good. Jump button good.
- Gameplay camera on portrait: character large, path visible. Fine. Sky/island framing okay. HUD coin counter with 0/75.

- Mobile title overlay: the bottom sign text "CLOUDTOP..." appears; fine. Play button good.
- Title controls show keyboard hints on touch device — should replace with touch instructions ("Joystick move · JUMP button"). Currently showing WASD/Space etc on mobile, not ideal. CSS could hide keyboard hints and show touch hint. Add an extra span in HTML with class "touch-only" saying "Drag to look around" and hide `.keyboard-only`? Simpler CSS for coarse pointer: `.title-controls` could show alternate text via pseudo-element? Better add a `<div class="title-controls title-controls--touch">` with joystick/jump/drag hints, hidden by default; show under coarse pointer; hide desktop controls. Implement.

- Also mobile title logo at 390: "3D" badge slightly cut on right (x up to ~390). In screenshot 3D badge fully visible? It's at right edge, seems just within. After reducing logo maybe fine. Add mobile font clamp smaller: currently clamp(52px, 10.2vw,108px) → 10.2vw at 390=40px, but clamp min 52 → 52px; CLOUD HOP ~9 chars at 52 with stroke 5 ≈ 340 + letterspacing; fits 390 with padding 16. The 3D badge positioned right -8 might clip 8px; set right: 6px on small screens. In screenshot 3D badge is fully visible though overlaps H? It looks fine.

- Mobile game HUD hearts look good; star counter "0/3". Coin 0/75; timer 0:00.5. Need pause button visible.

Let's fix HUD mobile CSS and touch hints.

Also title tagline on mobile wraps nicely.

Now, gameplay screen: the path ahead is at top of screen with coins. The camera is low; character center. Could increase pitch slightly on mobile based on aspect ratio to see more ahead? Maybe camera distance adjust to 8.2 for portrait. Not necessary.

Need ensure orientation landscape mobile HUD too. Test at 844x390 later.

Add CSS:
```
@media (max-width:700px){
 .hud{padding:12px}
 .hud__row{gap:4px}
 .heart{width:22px;height:21px}
 .star-counter{font-size:13px; padding:0 5px; gap:2px}
 .star-counter svg{width:14px}
 .coin-counter{font-size:19px;padding:2px 10px 2px 5px;gap:5px}
 .coin-icon{width:22px;height:22px;font-size:11px;border-width:2px}
 .coin-counter__total{font-size:11px}
 .timer{font-size:15px;min-width:56px}
 .icon-btn{width:32px;height:32px;border-radius:10px}
 .icon-btn svg{width:16px;height:16px}
 .hud__left,.hud__right{gap:4px}
}
```
But existing media max-width 700 has some styles; override within same block or add again later. Need hide course label already. Also center might take too much; add `.hud__center {flex:0 1 auto}`. On very narrow 360, still maybe. Hide mute button under 430px? Keep but compact. Let's compute 360: hearts 66 + star 38 = 104; center coin ~64; right timer 56 + buttons 32*2 + gaps 8 = 128; total 296 + row gaps 8 + padding 24 = 328 < 360. Fine.

Touch hint block:
```
<div class="title-controls title-controls--touch">
 <div class="control"><span>Drag anywhere</span><span>Look</span></div> ...
</div>
```
Better layout: "Left joystick move · JUMP jump · Drag look". Use `.title-controls--touch {display:none}`; @media hover none pointer coarse show and hide default by class `title-controls--keyboard`.
Add classes.

Also title "DRAG camera" currently. Fine.

Modify HTML title controls:
`<div class="title-controls title-controls--keyboard">...`
add touch one after.

CSS:
```
.title-controls--touch{display:none}
@media (hover:none) and (pointer:coarse){ .title-controls--keyboard{display:none} .title-controls--touch{display:flex} }
```
In current CSS, `.title-controls` has display flex; touch override hidden needs after.

Let's implement.

