  .title-card__tag { display: none; }
  .title-controls { display: none; }
  .title-card__foot { display: none; }
  .logo { transform: rotate(-1.5deg) scale(0.82); }
  .btn--play { margin-bottom: 0; }
}

@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
  *, *::before, *::after { animation-duration: 0.01ms !important; animation-iteration-count: 1 !important; transition-duration: 0.01ms !important; }
}

Append after media prefers-reduced-motion? Order: touch styles need override `.title-controls {display:none}` in max-height; if appended after, coarse pointer touch shows even in short viewport; maybe okay but could crowd. Better append before max-height block? Simpler append at end with media coarse; but max-height 560 hides title controls including touch; for landscape phones that's bad (844x390 gives no controls hints but still playable). Actually controls hint not essential. Keep.

Add base touch hidden before media, then coarse override at end. The `.title-controls` display flex default applies. Append:

```
.title-controls--touch {display:none}
...
@media (hover:none) and (pointer:coarse){ .title-controls--keyboard{display:none} .title-controls--touch{display:flex} }
```

And HUD mobile overrides. Append at end after reduced motion; media queries cascade fine. But `.title-controls--keyboard` base not display none; on desktop touch hidden. Good.

Let's append.

